Package: rsageExplore
Title: Exploration Guide Module for R Sage
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("R Sage contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@rsage.dev")
Description: Profiles a data frame and points to what is worth a closer
    look: the role and structure of each variable (IDs, scale items,
    repeated measures), distribution shapes, associations between
    variables, group differences, redundant variables, missingness that
    depends on other variables, and what goes with a chosen target
    variable. Each finding comes with its numbers, a small figure and a
    suggested next analysis. Numbers are computed here; the module does
    not fit or test the final models itself.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: rsage (>= 0.1.0), ggplot2, datawizard, rpart, cluster, stats, utils
Suggests: ranger, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
